<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Uganda minister at COP31: 'We need a just transition'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61ea5742d486842c2bc8e6e0b5958b70c6d0260fcf7d1cd898e2da3061753f9d</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209--312e033bb073.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Funding from wealthy countries to help deal with the impacts of climate change hasn't materialized, says Uganda's environment minister. The East African country is hoping oil and carbon credits will help boost finances.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan: Drones hit UN building, residential area in Khartoum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efe4ad101ef3b5137b37e08656fc9a053dd5f86ada8fdf6eab90b44fb4914dab</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T19:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sudan-drones-hit-un-building-residential-area-in-khartoum/a-80015122--86bdbc88b2b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-drones-hit-un-building-residential-area-in-khartoum/a-80015122?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The drones targeted Khartoum, damaging a UN building in the residential area. The UN agency deemed it unacceptable that humanitarian workers were exposed to such danger.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Libya: Suspected drone attack hits Russian ship in Benghazi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0981c48d68102e5589eff6d8f4fa478d486fa089438566cdb944742b99f810e6</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/libya-suspected-drone-attack-hits-russian-ship-in-benghazi/a-80014545--a60ea6375dca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/libya-suspected-drone-attack-hits-russian-ship-in-benghazi/a-80014545?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Russian vessel at an eastern Libyan naval base was hit by what is suspected to be a drone strike.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:229044eb65f29fe020e51c060c2c09d06a6ce00955bf9d10d2d64b446e7d10e6</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
